From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:35:48 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 335/335] Meridian: the tour's suggested spaces merge with the
 ones moved in from Arc
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Moving in from Arc brought Work and Home; the tour's setup from the apps
then added its own Work and Personal: Work, Home, Work, Personal.

The tour's suggestions (from the apps or from the AI) leave out a space
the person already has by that name, compared without case, emoji or
punctuation (SpaceNameKey: "💼 Work" is "work"), and one suggested
twice: the result is Work, Home, Personal. The proposal shown, the AI's
answer and ApplySetup all do it. A lone empty first space, which the
setup replaces, doesn't count; a space the person makes later may still
share a name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
